\title{aemet2fdata: Functional Data from AEMET OpenData}
\description{
Tools to download daily meteorological data from the AEMET OpenData API
and convert them into functional data objects (\code{fdata} and
\code{ldata}) for analysis with the \pkg{fda.usc} package.
}
\details{
Main functions:
\itemize{
\item \code{\link{aemet2inventory}}: station metadata (id, name,
province, altitude, longitude, latitude).
\item \code{\link{aemet2df}}: daily data as a base-R data.frame.
\item \code{\link{aemet2csv}}: whole daily history of each station,
requested in half-year windows, saved as one CSV (UTF-8) per station.
\item \code{\link{aemet2download}}: resumable bulk download (all
stations, long periods) to one file per station and year.
\item \code{\link{aemet2fdata}}: one variable as an \code{fdata} object
(one curve per station-year, 365 days).
\item \code{\link{aemet2lfdata}}: several variables as an \code{ldata}
object (a \code{df} with one row per curve plus one \code{fdata} per
variable).
}
An example data file is available at
\code{system.file("extdata", "aemet_example.csv", package = "aemet2fdata")}
(daily data of stations 1387, A Coruña, and B228, Palma Puerto, 2023-2024;
source: AEMET OpenData).

A personal API key is required to download data:
\url{https://opendata.aemet.es/centrodedescargas/altaUsuario}.

Other R packages also access AEMET OpenData, with different goals:
\pkg{climaemet} (many AEMET services, tidy and spatial output, climate
graphics) and \pkg{meteospain} (several Spanish meteorological services
with a common format). \pkg{aemet2fdata} focuses on long daily series
stored locally and on their conversion to functional data.

Data source: © AEMET (Agencia Estatal de Meteorología).
